---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Robert',
  url: 'https://bitevo.work/operator',
  jobTitle: 'Operator, BitEvo',
  affiliation: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'BitEvo',
    url: 'https://bitevo.work'
  },
  sameAs: ['https://github.com/bitmaster162']
};
---

<Layout
  title="Operator — BitEvo"
  description="Who runs BitEvo, what evidence is public, and what boundaries apply before an AI-agent authority validation engagement begins."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(structuredData)} />

  <section class="section operator-hero">
    <div class="container operator-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Public operator profile</div>
        <h1 class="display">Robert runs BitEvo.</h1>
        <p class="lede">BitEvo is an independent engineering practice focused on authority, evidence, external effects and recovery in action-capable AI-agent workflows.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/bitmaster162" rel="me">Public GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="button button-ghost" href="/proof">Review public proof</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="panel operator-card" aria-label="BitEvo operator summary">
        <div><small>OPERATOR</small><strong>Robert</strong></div>
        <div><small>AFFILIATION</small><strong>BitEvo</strong></div>
        <div><small>WORKING MODEL</small><strong>Independent · bounded engagements</strong></div>
        <div><small>DEFAULT SURFACE</small><strong>Public docs / synthetic / staging-test</strong></div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight section-rule">
    <div class="container split-head">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">What is publicly verifiable</div><h2 class="section-title">Claims are separated from evidence.</h2></div>
      <p class="lede">The public site intentionally distinguishes method, synthetic worked cases, internal dogfood and customer-independent engineering evidence. It does not present synthetic work as customer proof or imply certification.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="container proof-grid-small">
      <a class="panel proof-card" href="/proof"><span>01</span><h3>Proof matrix</h3><p>Worked synthetic cases and an explicit evidence-strength ladder.</p></a>
      <a class="panel proof-card" href="/dogfood-self-audit"><span>02</span><h3>Internal dogfood</h3><p>Bounded self-audit evidence, clearly labeled as internal rather than customer validation.</p></a>
      <a class="panel proof-card" href="/build"><span>03</span><h3>Build receipts</h3><p>Public engineering artifacts and quality gates that can be inspected independently.</p></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="container split-head">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">Engagement boundary</div><h2 class="section-title">Access is earned by scope, not assumed.</h2></div>
      <p class="lede">A first relevance check does not require production credentials, customer data or internal control-plane access. Public documentation and synthetic read-only examples are valid starting points when a team wants to evaluate the method before granting any deeper test surface.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="container boundary-list">
      <article><span>01</span><div><h3>Start public when possible</h3><p>Architecture claims, documentation and synthetic examples can establish whether a useful authority/evidence hypothesis exists.</p></div></article>
      <article><span>02</span><div><h3>Use staging/test for bounded validation</h3><p>Any active testing requires an agreed scope, explicit allowed actions and a non-production surface by default.</p></div></article>
      <article><span>03</span><div><h3>No unsolicited production access</h3><p>Credentials, production data, customer secrets and uncontrolled external effects are not prerequisites for an initial engagement.</p></div></article>
      <article><span>04</span><div><h3>Report only what evidence supports</h3><p>Findings are scoped to observed behavior, evidence quality, limitations and the owner decision they can justify.</p></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="container operator-cta panel">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">Commercial path</div><h2 class="section-title">Start with the smallest decision that matters.</h2><p class="lede">A free 20-minute triage checks fit. A $1,500 Entry Audit tests one critical action chain and one primary failure hypothesis. The broader $4,900 audit is for a multi-scenario authority decision.</p></div>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/pricing">See decision scopes →</a><a class="button" href="/agent-authority-audit">Read the method</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .operator-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.4fr) minmax(280px,.8fr); gap:clamp(2rem,6vw,5rem); align-items:center; }
  .operator-card { display:grid; gap:0; padding:0; overflow:hidden; }
  .operator-card div { display:grid; gap:.45rem; padding:1.15rem 1.35rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
  .operator-card div:last-child { border-bottom:0; }
  .operator-card small, .proof-card span, .boundary-list > article > span { color:var(--accent); font-size:.72rem; letter-spacing:.12em; }
  .operator-card strong { font-size:1rem; }
  .proof-grid-small { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:1rem; margin-top:2rem; }
  .proof-card { display:block; padding:1.4rem; text-decoration:none; color:inherit; }
  .proof-card h3 { margin:.8rem 0 .45rem; }
  .proof-card p { margin:0; color:var(--ink-soft); }
  .boundary-list { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1px; background:var(--line); border:1px solid var(--line); margin-top:2rem; }
  .boundary-list article { display:grid; grid-template-columns:2.5rem 1fr; gap:1rem; background:var(--bg); padding:1.35rem; }
  .boundary-list h3 { margin:0 0 .45rem; }
  .boundary-list p { margin:0; color:var(--ink-soft); }
  .operator-cta { padding:clamp(1.5rem,4vw,3rem); display:grid; gap:1.5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .operator-grid, .proof-grid-small, .boundary-list { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
  }
</style>
